P4 (issue #23, U12): the frequency repair of tbg_random also examines the
last item of its cyclic search.

The search for an under-represented item starts at a random index i and
stops at j = i-1 (cyclically) without examining item j, so a repair fails
when j is the only candidate. The patched test examines the item the
search stopped at. No random draw is added or removed.

--- a/tract/src/tract.c
+++ b/tract/src/tract.c
@@ -2721,7 +2721,7 @@
       while ((i != j)           /* and search cyclically from there */
       &&     ((ifrq[i].item & ITEM_MIN) || (ifrq[i].dif >= 0)))
         i = (i+1) % n;          /* find an under-represented item */
-      if (i != j) {             /* if under-represented item found */
+      if ((ifrq[i].dif < 0) && !(ifrq[i].item & ITEM_MIN)) { /* P4 */
         ifrq[*d].item &= ~ITEM_MIN;
         ifrq[*d    ].dif -= 1;  /* replace the over-represented item */
         ifrq[*d = i].dif += 1;  /* with the under-represented item */
